## Policy correction

The Daytona types reference and pinned `SandboxBaseParams` source document zero
as immediate stop/archive/delete, while zero disables auto-pause. Our current
generated `mapLifetimePolicies` now follows action-specific YAML rules:
disabled auto-pause maps to zero; immediate stop/archive/delete maps to zero.
Immediate auto-pause and explicit disabling of stop/archive/delete are rejected
before provider calls. Omitted/default policies stay omitted. An omitted native
field is not used to promise that provider defaults have been explicitly disabled.

## Documentation ambiguity

The Daytona client reference includes an image example using `Memory: 4096`
without stating units there. Sandbox field documentation explicitly states GiB.
That example alone is insufficient to change the existing memory conversion.
Request units should be checked against the API contract when revisiting it.

GPU, resizing, storage/volumes, harnesses, browsers, computer use, macOS/Windows,
and lifecycle operations remain future extensions. Tests use SDK service doubles
and a fake HTTP transport, with no live provisioning.

Daytona auto-pause supports explicit disabling (native zero), but cannot represent
an immediate pause. Stop/archive/delete support immediate AFTER zero; explicit
DISABLED for those actions is rejected, preserving provider default distinctions.
